{"name":"Black Pool","hex":"#4f5552","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"black pool","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A form of the game of pool, mainly played in the 19th century, which later merged with pyramid pool to become the game of snooker."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/black_pool"}],"entries":[{"title":"Black Pool","blocks":[{"text":"Black Pool is a hot spring in the West Thumb Geyser Basin of Yellowstone National Park in the United States."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Black_pool.jpg/330px-Black_pool.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Pool","wikidata":"Q4921486"},{"title":"Black pool","blocks":[{"text":"Black pool, originally known as everlasting pool, was a form of pocket billiards (pool) mainly played in the late 19th century, first being recorded in 1862. This game was derived from life pool but lacked the pooling of bets and players had unlimited lives. It had as many colour balls as players with an additional black ball that was placed on the centre spot. A player is paid a life (stake) from the opponent whose ball was potted. The player is then allowed to pot the black ball which meant all opponents must pay a life. Balls are respotted after being potted and the best strategy is to alternate potting colour and black to maximize money. Around 1875, black pool was merged with pyramid pool to form the new game of snooker, today one of the most popular cue sports in the world."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_pool","wikidata":"Q4922426"},{"title":"Black","blocks":[{"text":"Black is a color that results from the absence or complete absorption of visible light. It is an achromatic color, without chroma, like white and grey. It is often used symbolically or figuratively to represent darkness. Black and white have often been used to describe opposites such as good and evil, the Dark Ages versus the Age of Enlightenment, and night versus day. Since the Middle Ages, black has been the symbolic color of solemnity and authority, and for this reason it is still commonly worn by judges and magistrates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png/330px-Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black","wikidata":"Q23445"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/WestThumbGeyserBasin-BlackPool.jpg/500px-WestThumbGeyserBasin-BlackPool.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/WestThumbGeyserBasin-BlackPool.jpg/1280px-WestThumbGeyserBasin-BlackPool.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/WestThumbGeyserBasin-BlackPool.jpg/500px-WestThumbGeyserBasin-BlackPool.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWestThumbGeyserBasin-BlackPool.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Black_Pool_hot_spring_in_West_Thumb_Geyser_Basin.JPG/250px-Black_Pool_hot_spring_in_West_Thumb_Geyser_Basin.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Black_Pool_hot_spring_in_West_Thumb_Geyser_Basin.JPG/330px-Black_Pool_hot_spring_in_West_Thumb_Geyser_Basin.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Black_Pool_hot_spring_in_West_Thumb_Geyser_Basin.JPG/250px-Black_Pool_hot_spring_in_West_Thumb_Geyser_Basin.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":